        "original_id": "5b5e3925-b57a-5ea9-845e-9c610bb43e78",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Leigh Silverman, Jeanine Tesori, Brian Crawley, Doris Betts, David Henry Hwang, Jeff Locker\n- Works: Violet, From Up Here, Chinglish, The Ugliest Pilgrim\n- Roles: stage director, playwright, composer, librettist, actor\n- Awards: Tony Award, Drama Desk Award\n\nFacts:\n- Leigh Silverman is an American stage director who has worked both Off-Broadway and on Broadway.\n- In 2008, Leigh Silverman was nominated for the Drama Desk Award for Outstanding Director of a Play for From Up Here.\n- In 2011, Chinglish opened on Broadway with direction by Leigh Silverman.\n- Jeff Locker starred as Peter Timms in Chinglish, a play by David Henry Hwang.\n- In 2014, Leigh Silverman was nominated for the Tony Award for Best Direction of a Musical for Violet.\n- Violet is a musical with music by Jeanine Tesori and a libretto by Brian Crawley.\n- Violet is based on The Ugliest Pilgrim, a short story by Doris Betts.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
